                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital course of your 26-year-old female patient, admitted on 31/01/2020 with acute lower abdominal pain and confirmed tubal pregnancy. On admission, physical examination, transvaginal ultrasonography, and serum beta-hCG measurement confirmed a right-sided ectopic tubal pregnancy without signs of rupture. Given the clinical findings and hemodynamic stability, the patient underwent laparoscopic salpingectomy for removal of the ectopic pregnancy. The procedure was uneventful. Postoperatively, the patient recovered well, received appropriate analgesia and intravenous fluid support, and vital signs remained stable throughout. Wound care was provided prior to discharge. The patient was counseled regarding the implications for future fertility and advised on follow-up. She was discharged home on 02/02/2020 in good general condition. Please arrange outpatient follow-up as appropriate.</div>"
            },
